    static_gate: has 1 gate + L-shaped path but no marker; unchanged in output; 0-2 per grid
    static_marker: isolated single marker pixel on grid boundary; unchanged in output; 0-2 per grid
    counts: static_gate count == static_marker count; total components 1-6
  gate:
    structure: end(0)-center(3)-end(0) collinear triplet, axis horizontal or vertical
    placement: center always on grid boundary edge; axis parallel to that edge
    edges_used: 1-4 distinct edges host gates; left/top/bottom/right all possible
  path:
    shape: L-shaped (1 right-angle turn); arm1 (perpendicular to edge, from parking) 1-2 cells; arm2 (parallel to edge) 1-10 cells
    total_path_excl_gate: 2-11 cells
    parking: the unique path cell adjacent to gate center but not between the two ends
  marker:
    active_marker: adjacent to the far end of the L-path; always on grid boundary
    static_marker: isolated single cell on grid boundary, not adjacent to any path
  transform: for each active component, erase marker + all path cells except gate center, place marker at parking; static components unchanged
  separation: all components 4-connected-disjoint (min manhattan distance >= 2)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first (build settled state, then extend paths to get input)
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size H x W in [9,14].
    2. Decide component counts: N_active in [1,2], N_static_gate = N_static_marker in [0,2].
    3. For each component (active or static-gate), place a gate on a grid boundary edge.
       Gate = end-center-end triplet; center on edge, axis along edge. Ensure gates are well-separated.
    4. For each gate, determine parking cell (1 step inward from center, perpendicular to edge).
    5. For active components, place marker_color at parking (this is the output state).
    6. To build input, grow an L-shaped path from parking: arm1 extends 0-1 extra cells perpendicular to edge,
       then arm2 extends 1-10 cells parallel to edge. Place the marker adjacent to the far end of arm2
       (on the grid boundary). Remove marker from parking. This reverses the solver transform.
    7. For static-gate components, grow a similar L-path from parking (no marker needed).
    8. Place N_static_marker isolated marker pixels on the grid boundary, not adjacent to any component.
    9. Validate: all components are 4-connected-disjoint; no overlaps; solver recovers the output.
